    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: Temperament & Stress \u00a76 (CE-2272, R-2034) - three insurgents (the Insurgent type, obedience authored 0.3) hold their spots on open basic-desert, facing south (CombatPosture, stay; ROE StayOnTask - only a break moves him), a car 12 m behind each: the 'Coward' (nerve 0.1 - effective 0.22) at x 270, the 'Waverer' (resolve 0 - effective 0.15, under the 0.3 that surrenders) at x 340, the 'Fanatic' (resolve 1, nerve 0.9 - effective nerve 0.78) at x 520, out of the other riflemen's sight. Over each, 'Gunner <name>' (Friend automatic rifleman, InertSop) 120 m south fires 40 rounds, one every 1.3 s, 10 m behind him and 4 m up (near misses); the Coward and the Waverer each also have 'Rifleman <name>' (Friend rifleman, posted 55 m off watching him), who engages him - the rifle on him. All immortal. Judge (120 s): (1) the Coward breaks and runs (Break - to ground at cover farther from the fire), he does not surrender (effective resolve 0.5); (2) the Waverer breaks with a rifle on him and surrenders (hands up, weapons down); (3) the Fanatic never breaks or surrenders and fires back; (4) printed per insurgent: his peak stress, when he broke, what he did, the rounds he fired. Check: python3 scripts/utility-demo-check.py --launch ts-three-defenders. \ud83d\udcc4 docs/DESIGN_Temperament_And_Stress.md \u00a76"
  },
